[FINAL-TEXT] I have the root cause. The evidence is unambiguous — no need for further probes.

**Key findings:**

| Observation | Detail |
|---|---|
| pc_0_0 IP address | `10.0.0.2/24` ✓ correct |
| pc_0_0 default route | `default via **10.0.0.254** dev eth0` ← **wrong** |
| ARP for 10.0.0.254 | `(incomplete)` — no one owns that IP |
| ARP for 10.0.0.1 | resolves to `de:5e:c4:87:a2:12` ✓ (leaf_router_0_0 eth2) |
| leaf_router_0_0 eth2 | `10.0.0.1/24`, UP ✓ — fabric side is healthy |

The configured gateway (`10.0.0.254`) does not exist anywhere in the fabric. The ARP for it is permanently `(incomplete)`, so every packet that requires the default route is silently dropped. Pings to `10.0.0.1` succeed purely because that destination falls inside the directly-attached connected route (`10.0.0.0/24 dev eth0`), bypassing the default gateway entirely.

